the main difference between the .env file and the config folder is that the config folder provides the base and default paramters and the default settings of each and every config file/setting that we will use in our project.  the env file provides the actual values that we want to use instead of the default settings the env is given the prority follwed by the default config in the config folder for eg if the database name and the connection is defined in the env file then the env files connection will be used by the laravel or the by default database setting in the config database file will be used.

 
It is not advisiable to use assing the env variables direclty in the program as we can do it in the .env file which if done directy in the program it exposes the risk of the creadentials and private data to be get stolen or attacked and stole by the attacker there .env should be considered instead of hardcoding the credentials directly in the database.

the php artisan config:cache is used to clear the configuration cache i.e all related to sessions and the .env file the draw back is that 
the sessions and all the connections and the cache data clears in this case.


if the database is changed in the .env file and the database is still connecting to the database in the either it might be using the config default database as fallback if the new database connection is set by wrong credentials or paramters or the cache of existing config settings might be still present in such case we have to use the config clear database.


we should never commit the .env file to the github as it contains all the important credentails that we are going to use in the live system.
